// WindowProxy is an ECMAScript exotic object, not a WebIDL interface
// See: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#the-windowproxy-exotic-object
//
// From the spec:
// "There is no WindowProxy interface object."
// "A WindowProxy is an exotic object that wraps a Window ordinary object"
//
// In WebIDL type positions, WindowProxy is used to represent a reference to
// a browsing context's window that may change across navigations.
//
// For implementation purposes, we treat WindowProxy as an alias to Window.
// The actual exotic object behavior is implemented by the JavaScript engine,
// not by WebIDL bindings.

typedef Window WindowProxy;
